    "brute": {
      "word": "BRUTE",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "Not having sensation; senseless; inanimate; unconscious; without intelligence or volition; as, the brute earth; the brute powers of nature.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "Not possessing reason, irrational; unthinking; as, a brute beast; the brute creation. A creature . . . not prone And brute as other creatures, but endued With sanctity of reason. Milton.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "Of, pertaining to, or characteristic of, a brute beast. Hence: Brutal; cruel; fierce; ferocious; savage; pitiless; as, brute violence. Macaulay. The influence of capital and mere brute labor. Playfair.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "Having the physical powers predominating over the mental; coarse; unpolished; unintelligent. A great brute farmer from Liddesdale. Sir W. Scott.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "Rough; uncivilized; unfeeling. [R.]",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "An animal destitute of human reason; any animal not human; esp. a quadruped; a beast. Brutes may be considered as either aëral, terrestrial, aquatic, or amphibious. Locke.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A brutal person; a savage in heart or manners; as unfeeling or coarse person. An ill-natured brute of a husband. Franklin.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "To report; to bruit. [Obs.]",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        }
      ],
